ing everyone with something like Medicare for all\".\n  - 2026-05-15 CBS debate: he says he has been a proponent and author of Medicare for All legislation.\n  - 2026-02-10 Commonwealth Club forum: he has been a supporter of Medicare for all \"for decades\".\n- **Other passages, coded but not counted:**\n  - His health-care issue page shows only which side he is on. It is also undated.\n  - The 2026-09-30 remarks on Medicaid work requirements are `adjacent`.\n- **Annex conflict:** the annex has a proposed line saying a state officeholder's rung 1 is `scope-unavailable`. I followed the newer 2026-10-06 ruling instead: a level with no lever is limited to own words, not excluded. Someone should reconcile the annex.\n- **Possible misreading:** at least one of these answers came in reply to a question about single-payer in California. The annex says a state single-payer plan is not Medicare. I seated rung 1 because his words name Medicare and everyone, and he ties them to his federal bills. A reviewer could reasonably read this as BLANK `direction-only` instead.","ttft_ms":25719,"type":"result","duration_ms":52877,"uuid":"87a52525-1200-480b-b732-9247404758ee","ttft_stream_ms":2147,"time_to_request_ms":80,"first_content_frame_ms":2147,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
